        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "All national parks are great to see, but Yellowstone was the world’s first in 1872! It is in the United States. The name was "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "taken from",
            "zh": "取自"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the Yellowstone River. It "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "flows through",
            "zh": "流经"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the park."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "★ People go to Yellowstone to see "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Old Faithful",
            "zh": "老忠实泉"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "shoots",
            "ref": "v-shoot"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " hot water 30 metres high about every 90 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "★ Many kinds of animals live in the park."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "● The "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bison",
            "zh": "野牛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is the biggest "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "land animal",
            "zh": "陆生动物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "North America",
            "zh": "北美洲"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Thousands of bison live in Yellowstone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "● The next-biggest animals in the park are "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "grizzly bears",
            "zh": "灰熊"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They are fast for their size."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "● Over 100 years ago, wolves were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "forced",
            "ref": "v-force"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " out of Yellowstone. Later, people brought them back."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "★ Native Americans* lived in Yellowstone long before it became a national park. Old "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "shelters",
            "zh": "居所"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " still stand in the park today."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "* Native American 北美土著人，印第安人"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
